{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And to the entrance of the Tent of Meeting.</b> All the while that Moses had not set up the Tabernacle, offerings were brought in any place, and so we find: ״וישלח את נערי בני ישראל ויעלו עולות״. Once the Tabernacle was erected, they were warned and forbidden to sacrifice except at the entrance of the Tent of Meeting. <b>Dam (blood) — it shall be counted.</b> The verse speaks of unconsecrated meat, to accustom them to withdraw their hands from idolatry, as it goes on to explain: ״ולא יזבחו עוד את זבחיהם לשעירים״ — for they were steeped in these in Egypt, and now He commanded that they make their unconsecrated meat into peace-offerings." "<b>He shed blood and shall be cut off.</b> For he shed blood that he should have sprinkled before HaShem." "<b>He shed blood and shall be cut off.</b> We have heard the punishment; from where is the warning? The verse teaches: ״השמר לך פן תעלה עולותיך״ etc."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:13:03.873186172Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}